Description: WiFi setup for a Raspberry Pi over Bluetooth, keyed by its LED
 rpiledconfig lets the RPi LED Config phone app set a Raspberry Pi's WiFi
 over Bluetooth LE. When a phone connects it draws a one-time 64-bit key and
 blinks it on the Pi's activity LED; the phone reads it with its camera and
 proves it with SPAKE2, and the WiFi network and passphrase then go over an
 encrypted channel to NetworkManager.
 .
 The service runs as rpiledconfig.service, as its own unprivileged user, and
 advertises for as long as it runs; /etc/rpiledconfig/rpiledconfig.conf says
 otherwise. /usr/share/doc/rpiledconfig/security.md says what that exposes.
